  "designPrinciples": [
    "Model functional behavior rather than physical wiring topology.",
    "Keep water delivery, circulation, drainage, heating, drying, sensing, control, and door authorization diagnostically distinct.",
    "Manufacturer-specific pump architectures, heater implementations, drying systems, diverter systems, and communication topologies belong in overlays.",
    "Command evidence must remain distinct from load operation evidence.",
    "Water fill must be established before diagnosing circulation-dependent faults.",
    "Drain completion must be established before treating residual water as a circulation or heating problem.",
    "Heating command, heater current, and temperature response are separate evidence stages.",
    "Normal operation is not proof of component health.",
    "Ranking does not constitute component verification.",
    "Do not encode every hose, channel, manifold, check valve, or sump passage in the canonical graph — those emerge in overlays when diagnostically relevant."
  ],
